pckt (0.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add DHCPv6, NetBIOS name service, SSDP, 802.3 LLC/SNAP and CDP
    layers, and decode LLMNR as DNS.
  * Port pypcap3's features into pckt.pcap: dispatch(), iteration,
    capture files through Dumper, open_dead(), compiled and raw BPF
    programs, more capture settings, nanosecond timestamps, Ctrl-C to
    interrupt blocked reads, and a type stub.
  * Fix 'ip broadcast' filters on live handles, which were given the
    device's netmask in the wrong byte order.
  * Treat a truncated DHCP option as malformed rather than raising
    IndexError.
  * Remove ghost (pckt.stack) and the passive mapper (pckt.mapping),
    which are separate projects now.
  * Move the layer7 modules into pckt: pckt.layer7.dns is now pckt.dns.

 -- Matthew Shaw <mshaw.cx@gmail.com>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:45:27 -0400

pckt (0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Map hosts from IPv6 neighbor discovery, mDNS and LLDP in the passive
    mapper, with a new LLDP layer.
  * Guess the OS of more DHCP clients: Android, busybox and dhcpcd by
    their vendor class, and Apple and Windows clients by the options
    they request.
  * findalldevs() lists every IPv4 and IPv6 address of each interface.
  * Fail rather than report macOS's placeholder MAC to processes that
    aren't root.
  * Require Python 3.11.

 -- Matthew Shaw <mshaw.cx@gmail.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:57:14 -0400

